# LOOM Repository .gitignore

# Secrets and credentials (NEVER commit)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
secrets.json
credentials.json
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx

# GitHub Copilot
.copilot_token
COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN

# AWS / Azure / GCP credentials
~/.aws/
~/.azure/
~/.gcp/

# IDE & editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Node / NPM
node_modules/
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Build artifacts
_site/
_build/
dist/
build/

# Temporary / cache
.cache/
*.tmp
*.temp

# LOOM-specific (do not commit Masco data)
# If you accidentally add Masco files, add patterns here
/masco/
/internal/
secrets/

# GitHub Actions logs (auto-generated)
.github/workflows/logs/

# Do not commit project status files (these are auto-generated by workflows)
registry/census-latest.md
registry/repos.yaml
_data/briefs/

# Lock files from template projects (if any)
Pipfile.lock
poetry.lock

# Misc
*.log
*.bak
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

---

## IMPORTANT: Data Boundary Check

Before committing, ask yourself:
- [ ] Is there Masco code, credentials, or identities in this commit?
- [ ] Are there tenant IDs, app IDs, or customer data?
- [ ] Are there internal roadmaps, pricing, or strategy from Masco?

If yes to any of the above: **DO NOT COMMIT**. Delete the files and add their pattern to this .gitignore.

LOOM is personal to Justin. Masco data stays in Masco repos.
